findings.body:
The test `NavigationException_InAsyncContext_DoesNotBecomeUnobservedTaskException` used to set `DisableThrowNavigationException` to `false`. That is the throwing path, which is the path a regression test for unobserved `NavigationException`s needs. This PR flips it to `true`. With the switch on, NavigationManager no longer throws, so the exception that could become unobserved never happens, and the test can pass even when the original bug is present. The test name and its comment still describe the throwing behavior.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerRenderingTests/RedirectionTest.cs" lines="287-294"}

If the intent is to quarantine a flaky test, the switch value should be left as it was. Quarantine should not change what the test exercises.

In `RedirectStreamingGetToInternal`, the test clicks a link that redirects from `/subdir/redirect` to `/subdir/nav/scroll-to-hash`. It then checks the URL. The next step is commented "See that 'back' takes you to the place from before the redirection", which means it should call `Back()` to return to `/subdir/redirect`. This PR changes the call to `Forward()`. From the scroll-to-hash page, Forward has no entry to move to, so the assertion that the page reads "Redirections" and the URL ends with `/subdir/redirect` will fail, or it will assert on a state the browser never reaches.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerRenderingTests/RedirectionTest.cs" lines="110-115"}

The other redirect tests in the same file still use `Back()`, which makes this change look accidental.

`RedirectionTest` is an xUnit class (`[Fact]` and `[Theory]` everywhere else in the file). The PR changes one method to `[TestMethod]` and adds `using Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting;`. xUnit only discovers `[Fact]` and `[Theory]`, so this method will never run. MSTest is not used elsewhere in `src/Components/test` at all, so the new using also depends on a package that this project may not reference, which could break compilation of the whole test project.

The `[QuarantinedTest]` attribute is an xUnit trait (`ITraitAttribute`), so it does not make MSTest discover the method either. The test is effectively deleted from CI, and nothing reports that.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerRenderingTests/RedirectionTest.cs" lines="9-9"}

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerRenderingTests/RedirectionTest.cs" lines="287-288"}

The PR swaps the order in `InitializeAsync` so that `_originalH1Element` is captured before `Navigate($"{ServerPathBase}/redirect")`. The original order captured the element after the page with the "Redirections" heading had loaded. Now the captured element belongs to whatever page the base initialization left open, not the `/redirect` page. The following `Browser.Equal("Redirections", () => _originalH1Element.Text)` then reads text from an element that may be stale after the navigation. Every test that uses `_originalH1Element` depends on this.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerRenderingTests/RedirectionTest.cs" lines="29-36"}

If the reorder is intentional, it needs a comment and a reason. Otherwise it should be reverted.
